[thin] Wrong material-thickness classification: these two exact segments cross the authored 0.25 mm open interval between Y96.836 and Y97.086. Native and actual fluted-STL samples leave material in each reported direction. The 0.575/0.601 mm endpoint distances are not continuous wall sections.
alternatives: Require material occupancy along the segment before classifying thickness. Filling this interval would remove the sliding clearance.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-bottom.step
click: x=-94.345 y=96.694 z=160.000
click: x=94.402 y=96.701 z=160.000

[thin] Wrong material-thickness classification: these rounded rail-entry corner segments cross air before reaching a neighboring face. Native and actual fluted-STL quarter, midpoint and later samples are outside material. The 2.629/2.648 mm endpoint distances do not measure continuous material.
alternatives: Require continuous material along the segment or retain its separate occupied intervals. Filling the opening would change the rail-entry and corner clearance.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-bottom.step
click: x=88.753 y=16.839 z=15.650
click: x=88.753 y=16.839 z=152.250

[thin] Specific cosmetic-flute profile exception: these are true short chords across the authored exterior groove/land contour and entry fade. Five interior samples of every listed segment lie in the actual final fluted STL. The shared profile is 4 mm wide and 1.2 mm deep, with a 5 mm smoothstep fade; current pitch is 4.9338 mm. The corner coupon and full-front photographs in cadlib/flute-evidence/README.md establish their profile and appearance scopes. This is a specific exterior-texture allowance, with no 3 mm finished-wall, exact current-field deposition, surface-quality or load-capacity acceptance.
alternatives: Flattening or shallowing changes the retained visible profile. Widening the lands changes the closed field spacing. Assess a finish change against the appearance evidence; a thickness-only cutoff cannot choose that contour.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-front-bottom.step
